# Third-party reference material stays out of Wingman's history.
#
# The rule sits at the top of the pen rather than inside each package folder.
# A nested guard covers only the directory it lives in, so a package extracted
# beside `EasySchematic/`, or an `extracted/` written straight into here,
# reached the index with nothing to stop it. Git applies this file to
# everything below it, which is the whole pen.
#
# Everything is ignored, and each note worth keeping is re-opened by name. A
# directory is re-opened before the file inside it, because git will not
# re-include a file whose parent it has already excluded — so the directory
# line is load-bearing rather than tidiness.
*
!/.gitignore
!/EasySchematic/
!/EasySchematic/README.md
